<div class="page">
  <div class="top-bar">
    <div>
      <div class="sub">IBM watsonx Challenge 2026 · Growth Enablers Track · Sales Committee</div>
      <h1>ISC Automated Sales Forecast</h1>
      <div class="sub">AI-powered GM meeting prep — 90 min → under 5 min, every week</div>
    </div>
    <div class="badge">v2.6.3-rc1 · Path 1: Built During Challenge</div>
  </div>

  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">94%</div><div class="stat-l">Time reduction</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">90→5</div><div class="stat-l">Minutes per week</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">9</div><div class="stat-l">IBM users, live</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">51</div><div class="stat-l">Sessions w/ IBM Bob</div></div>
  </div>

  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>Every week, US Public Sector IBM Sales VP <strong>Dushyant K. Patel</strong> spends 60–90 minutes manually preparing for his GM meeting: opening IBM Sales Cloud (ISC), exporting pipeline data to a spreadsheet, hand-scoring each deal, writing a narrative summary from memory, and formatting a PowerPoint. The process is slow, error-prone, and memory-dependent — and it repeats every single week of every quarter.</p>
  <p>IBM Sales Cloud is protected by IBM w3id SSO with passkey authentication, blocking all programmatic access. Seven documented technical approaches — SAQL API, Playwright automation, browser extensions, Salesforce Connected App — all failed. The data was locked inside an authenticated browser session with no extraction path.</p>

  <h2>The Solution</h2>
  <p><strong>ISC Automated Sales Forecast</strong> replaces that 90-minute workflow with a single five-minute, AI-powered process. The key insight: a browser HAR file captures authenticated API responses directly — turning IBM's own security posture into a feature. One HAR export, one click, and the entire pipeline is loaded, scored, narrativized, diff'd, and ready to present.</p>

  <div class="two-col">
    <ul class="feat">
      <li><span class="icon">⟳</span><div><span class="lbl">Refresh Data</span><span class="dsc">HAR import loads full pipeline in &lt;2 sec. Each user's rows isolated by IBM ID.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="icon">⬡</span><div><span class="lbl">Score with watsonx</span><span class="dsc">ibm/granite-13b scores every deal 0–100. Rule-based fallback when offline.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="icon">✍</span><div><span class="lbl">GM Narrative</span><span class="dsc">llama-3-70b writes meeting-ready opening paragraph + bullets scoped to current filter.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="icon">⇄</span><div><span class="lbl">What Changed</span><span class="dsc">Diff engine compares live vs. saved baseline: new deals, stage changes, slippage, amount shifts.</span></div></li>
    </ul>
    <ul class="feat">
      <li><span class="icon">📊</span><div><span class="lbl">Baseline &amp; GM Report</span><span class="dsc">One click: immutable baseline written + IBM-branded PPTX downloaded with narrative + diff slide.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="icon">📋</span><div><span class="lbl">Custom PPT Column Picker</span><span class="dsc">User picks columns, drags to reorder, generates tailored PPTX in seconds.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="icon">♥</span><div><span class="lbl">Deal Health Card</span><span class="dsc">Hygiene score (0–100), P1/P2/P3 action items, week-over-week timeline per deal.</span></div></li>
      <li><span class="icon">⇅</span><div><span class="lbl">Multi-Column Sort</span><span class="dsc">Up to 6 stacked sort keys with group-by divider rows. Turns pipeline into analytical workspace.</span></div></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Business Impact</h2>
  <div class="callout green">
    <strong>Client Zero:</strong> IBM using its own watsonx technology to transform an internal IBM sales workflow before recommending it to clients. Dushyant Patel's HCLS team within US Public Market IBM is the first production user. The same weekly workflow — forecast review, rep hygiene coaching, GM meeting prep — runs in every IBM geography and every sales segment.
  </div>
  <p>Beyond the primary user: 9 IBM TSLs, ATLs, and the GM/VP are fully provisioned with isolated pipelines. The Pipeline Intelligence Engine surfaces rep coaching signals — blank Next Steps, stale close plans, forecast mismatches — that a VP typically discovers only when it's too late. The permanent quarterly audit ledger creates an SR/SM/Customer trajectory dataset that didn't exist before.</p>

