<div class="page">
  <div class="top-bar">
    <div>
      <div class="sub">Technical Architecture</div>
      <h1>ISC Automated Sales Forecast</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="badge">v2.6.3-rc1</div>
  </div>

  <h2>Architecture Overview</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technology</th><th>Role</th></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Frontend</strong></td><td>Vanilla JS · IBM Carbon Design System · IBM Plex Sans</td><td>Status-driven action bar, filter bar, modals, drag-to-reorder Column Picker, sort modal, Deal Health Card</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Server</strong></td><td>Node.js 18 · Express · express-session</td><td>All API endpoints, auth middleware, HAR ingestion trigger, PPT generation orchestration</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Database</strong></td><td>SQLite · better-sqlite3</td><td>opportunities, baseline_ledger, users, sessions — all tables keyed by user_id for multi-tenant isolation</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Auth</strong></td><td>Simulated IBM SSO · bcryptjs · OIDC-ready architecture</td><td>Session shape identical to real IBM w3id OIDC — swap to production requires 1 code block + 2 env vars</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>AI — Scoring</strong></td><td>ibm/granite-13b-instruct-v2 via watsonx.ai</td><td>0–100 confidence score per deal; rule-based fallback when credentials unavailable</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>AI — Narrative</strong></td><td>meta-llama/llama-3-70b-instruct via watsonx.ai</td><td>GM meeting opening paragraph + bullets scoped to current filtered view</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>AI — Delta</strong></td><td>ibm/granite-3-8b-instruct via watsonx.ai</td><td>Week-over-week change summary for What Changed slide</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>PPT</strong></td><td>pptxgenjs</td><td>IBM-branded PPTX: cover + data slides + What Changed. Dynamic column widths for Column Picker output.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Data ingestion</strong></td><td>HAR parser (custom · scraper/load-from-har.js)</td><td>Extracts SAQL API responses from browser HAR — the only viable path past IBM w3id passkey auth</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Key Engineering Decisions</h2>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <p><strong>HAR ingestion over API scraping:</strong> IBM Sales Cloud blocks every programmatic access path. The HAR file captures authenticated browser responses — no credentials stored in the app, no security risk, no IBM IT approval required to get started.</p>
      <p><strong>Append-only baseline ledger:</strong> Every "Confirm &amp; Generate" writes an immutable UUID-keyed row-set to baseline_ledger. No DELETE or UPDATE paths exist. A strict <code>confirmed_at &lt; asOf</code> SQL guard makes "today vs today" diff structurally impossible — the same discipline as an auditable financial system.</p>
      <p><strong>Column Picker PPT:</strong> COLUMN_META map drives dynamic proportional width calculation across all 12 fields. generateCustomPpt() scales defaultW weights to fill exactly 13.0" — no hardcoded column widths. Uses filtered.filter(selected) — the same guard that fixed the 943-vs-21 row bug on the main PPT button.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p><strong>Pipeline Intelligence Engine:</strong> Hygiene scoring (0–100) built from the existing schema — no new data sources. Padded-close detection flags deals within 4 days of quarter-end (P1/P2/P3). Manager-grouped Rep Hygiene Summary with rep drill-down modal. All rules-based; watsonx upgrade path documented in server/hygieneScore.js.</p>
      <p><strong>Multi-tenant data isolation:</strong> Every DB table keyed by user_id. PPT output namespaced to output/{ibm_id}/. Sessions per-user. Zero cross-user data leakage possible by schema design, not just by access control.</p>
      <p><strong>Day 0 reset utility:</strong> scripts/day0-reset.js wipes all 9 users and re-seeds 54 deals + 9 confirmed baselines in &lt;2 seconds. --dry-run flag previews before writing. Enables reproducible demo and video recording from a known-good state.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Build Process</h2>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Built entirely with IBM Bob</strong> across 51 sessions (~100 hours, July 10–21, 2026). Every design decision, architecture choice, debugging session, and line of production code was collaborative with IBM's own watsonx AI development tool. The complete session log — UCC1-TechnicalSessionLog.md — is part of the repository: an unedited technical history of an IBMer and IBM Bob building a production application together.
  </div>

  <h2>Test Coverage</h2>
  <p><strong>34/34 assertions passing</strong> — scripts/test-baseline-ledger.js runs a full 13-week Q3 2026 in-memory simulation: baseline writes, diff computation, "today vs today" guard, quarter boundaries, multi-user isolation. Passes in under 5 seconds on any Node.js 18+ machine.</p>

